# Security Guidelines

## Mandatory Security Checks

Before ANY commit:
- [ ] No hardcoded secrets (API keys, passwords, tokens, Supabase service role)
- [ ] All user inputs validated (Zod at boundaries)
- [ ] Injection prevention (parameterized queries / Supabase client APIs — never string-built SQL)
- [ ] XSS prevention (no unsanitized HTML)
- [ ] Auth/authorization verified when endpoints mutate data
- [ ] Error messages don't leak sensitive data

## Secret Management

- NEVER hardcode secrets in source code
- ALWAYS use environment variables (see `.env.example`)
- Only `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` values may ship to the client — treat them as public
- Validate that required server secrets are present where used
- Rotate any secrets that may have been exposed

## Portfolio-specific

- Supabase **anon** key may be `NEXT_PUBLIC_` when RLS protects data
- Supabase **service role** key is server-only — never prefix with `NEXT_PUBLIC_`
- R2 CDN base URL is public (`NEXT_PUBLIC_R2_CDN_URL`); never put R2 access keys in this consume-only app

## Security Response Protocol

If a security issue is found:
1. STOP immediately
2. Use the security-review skill / process
3. Fix CRITICAL issues before continuing
4. Rotate any exposed secrets
5. Review the codebase for similar issues
